Maybe change this into this:

```suggestion
    expect(classes.get('a')?.styles).toEqual(['stroke-width: 8px']);
    expect(classes.get('b')?.styles).toEqual(['stroke-width: 8px']);
```

To be consistent everywhere.

I'm not a big fan of using the `!` non-null assertion since it can hide bugs.

Would something like the following be better:

```suggestion
  let foundClass = classes.get(id);
  if (foundClass === undefined) {
    foundClass = { id: id, styles: [], textStyles: [] };
    classes.set(id, foundClass); // This is a classDef
  }
```

I've got a big list of minor refactoring changes in https://github.com/mermaid-js/mermaid/commit/730fa89e4c0b9ba81a6242753f8c78c71cce4174 that you're welcome to merge into this branch too.
